maria_cs: Heads-up: Monolith onboarding seeing a burst of 429s on the preflight step when they spin up CI (spike ~600 req/s). Tokens all look identical across containers.
priya_se: On it. Are they using the browser SDK or server-side warmup? Can you paste a sample request header and the error body?
maria_cs: Server-side Node SDK in a mono-repo. Calls /v1/embeddings during build. Gateway returns 429 rate_limit_exceeded. Log snippet shows repeated token iat and identical x-client-id across workers — looks like no splay.
sam_eng: From infra side: their refresh is synchronous across ~30 worker processes. They all request new ephemeral tokens at TTL boundary and then preflight fanout. Recommend splaying token refresh + client jitter. Also consider temporary increase to circuit-breaker bucket for ramp window.
maria_cs: Customer asked for an actionable playbook they can drop into CI to avoid the outage during ramp — want sample snippets and rollback steps.
sam_eng: Suggested minimal changes to ship quickly:
```js
// pseudo-config for Node CI workers
const SPLAY_MS = Math.floor(Math.random() * 5000); // 0-5s random start
setTimeout(async () => { await fetchToken(); startWorker(); }, SPLAY_MS);

// exponential backoff with full jitter on preflight failures
async function preflight() {
  for (let i=0;i<5;i++) {
    try { return await callPreflight(); }
    catch(e) {
      const backoff = Math.pow(2,i) * 100 + Math.random()*100;
      await sleep(backoff);
    }
  }
  throw new Error('preflight failed after retries');
}
```
sam_eng: Also add header-level sampling in their telemetry so we can correlate x-client-id, container id, and token iat.
priya_se: Recommend shared short-lived cache if containers co-located (redis/memcached) — reuse token until ~80% of TTL then leader refreshes. If they can't introduce cache, leader election (one process refreshes, others poll).
maria_cs: Good. I'll include a one-page playbook: 1) add startup splay 0-5s, 2) jittered backoff on preflight, 3) optional token cache or leader refresh, 4) experiment: increase per-client bucket for first 2 minutes.
maria_cs: Which request headers should I ask them to attach for triage?
sam_eng: Request: full preflight request headers (redact keys), including Authorization token (show iat/exp but redact token), x-client-id, x-region, container-id, and the raw response body. Also CPU/mem at time of spike.
priya_se: I'll draft the email and include a curl reproducer and rollback steps (pause parallel jobs, add 200ms startup jitter, ramp to 10% workers per minute). :thumbsup:
maria_cs: Thanks — I'll send that now and schedule a check-in tomorrow morning. :pray:
